# Federation ordnance.
#
# The mod registered ZERO torpedo types of its own, so every armed Federation hull listed
# `Homing` and nothing else - a Galaxy and a Defiant fired the same generic round as a
# TSN light cruiser. Reported from the playtest: "The Federation should have Photon
# Torpedoes instead of homing. They should be stronger than homing."
#
# A type is nothing but a shared string keyed by an arbitrary name, and the type set is
# not fixed by the engine - `Tag`, `PShock` and `Beacon` are themselves mod-added types
# that did not exist in stock, which is the existence proof that this is allowed.
#
# `player_ship_roles: federation`, NOT `tsn`. LegendaryMissions gates every one of its own
# types on `tsn`, and a ship's SIDE is a role - so TNG crews, who are side `federation`,
# were never granted PShock, Tag or Beacon either. These three are granted to the side
# this mod's players actually fly.
#
# The scale they sit on, from LM: Homing 35 standard, EMP 50 blast+reduce_shields,
# Nuke 5 blast. Photon is the new baseline; the other two are meant to be scarce.

# CREATE THEM. A type label is inert until it is spawned - `prefab_torpedo_type` is what
# calls `torpedo_type()` and registers the shared string the engine reads for damage,
# warhead, speed and colour. LegendaryMissions spawns its own seven in server_console;
# nothing was spawning these three, so a Federation hull carried Photon ROUNDS out of its
# `torpedostart` while the engine had no definition of what a Photon is.
#
# ORDER DOES NOT MATTER, which is worth knowing before worrying about it:
# `prefab_torpedo_type` grants the type to every player ship that ALREADY exists, and
# LM's `//spawn` route grants every registered type to ships that arrive LATER. Whichever
# way round the two happen, a ship ends up with its rounds.
# ONLY IF THE REGISTRAR IS LOADED. Each type below ends in `jump prefab_torpedo_type`,
# and that label belongs to LegendaryMissions, not to this add-on. A jump to a label
# nothing defines is NOT a compile error - it compiles clean and fails only when it runs
# - so without this guard the mod's own viewer, which loads sbs_utils and tng_races and
# nothing else, threw three runtime errors and reported FAIL on every headless run.
#
# Deliberately NOT a `requires`. A hard dependency here would take every mission that
# loads tng_races without LM to zero labels, which is the exact failure LM's hangar
# add-on caused across 22 missions. Optional, guarded, and it says so out loud.
tng_torpedo_registrar = tng_has_label("prefab_torpedo_type")
if tng_torpedo_registrar:
    prefab_spawn(tng_prefab_photon_torpedo)
    prefab_spawn(tng_prefab_quantum_torpedo)
    prefab_spawn(tng_prefab_tricobalt_device)
else:
    # print, not log: log() is Python logging with no handler attached and is invisible
    # in the engine, and this is the only report that the Federation is flying without
    # its own ordnance.
    print("tng_races: prefab_torpedo_type not loaded - Photon, Quantum and Tricobalt "
          "NOT registered. Load the LegendaryMissions prefabs add-on to get them.")


=== tng_prefab_photon_torpedo
metadata: ```
key: Photon
gui_name: Photon
sort_order: 0
speed: 12
lifetime: 25
flare_color: red
trail_color: #f84
warhead: standard
blast_radius: 1000
damage: 50
explosion_size: 12
explosion_color: fire
behavior: homing
energy_conversion_value: 100
default_max_count: 10
player_ship_roles: federation
build_times:
    command: 2
    civil: 6
    industry: 1
    science: 6
    default: 3
```
    jump prefab_torpedo_type


=== tng_prefab_quantum_torpedo
metadata: ```
key: Quantum
gui_name: Quantum
sort_order: 1
speed: 12
lifetime: 25
flare_color: #9cf
trail_color: #48f
warhead: blast,reduce_shields
blast_radius: 1200
damage: 75
explosion_size: 18
explosion_color: #9cf
behavior: homing
energy_conversion_value: 200
default_max_count: 4
player_ship_roles: quantum_armed
build_times:
    command: 4
    civil: 12
    industry: 3
    science: 12
    default: 6
```
    # "Like a nuke with EMP built in" - and that is expressible natively, with no script
    # at all: `warhead` is comma-combinable, so `blast,reduce_shields` IS a blast that
    # also strips shields. LM's own EMP already uses that warhead but with 50 damage
    # instead of real damage; this one hits like a torpedo AND takes the shields down.
    #
    # FOUR ROUNDS, not ten. A weapon that does both jobs at once stops being a decision
    # if you have a magazine full of them.
    #
    # AND NOT ON EVERY HULL. `quantum_armed` rather than `federation`: quantum torpedoes
    # were late-era and never general issue, so the //spawn route below puts them on the
    # Sovereign, the Defiant and the Galaxy refit. Gated on the SIDE they would have been
    # standard on a Constellation, which is the wrong century.
    jump prefab_torpedo_type


