    command: 8
    civil: 20
    industry: 6
    science: 20
    default: 12
```
    # VOYAGER ONLY, which is why this one is gated on a role rather than on the side. A
    # tricobalt device is not standard Federation ordnance - it is the thing a ship
    # seventy thousand light years from home uses when it has run out of better ideas -
    # so the //spawn route at the end of this file puts `tricobalt_armed` on the
    # Intrepid hull and on nothing else.
    #
    # Slow, enormous, and two rounds. The blast radius is 2.5x a photon's, so it is as
    # dangerous to a careless helm as it is to the target.
    jump prefab_torpedo_type


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Voyager gets the tricobalt, and nobody else does.
#
# The role has to be ON the ship before LegendaryMissions' own //spawn route walks the
# registered types and grants the ones whose `player_ship_roles` match. Two spawn routes
# racing over one ship is not something to rely on, so this does not rely on it: it adds
# the role AND grants the rounds itself, which is idempotent either way -
# `torpedo_make_available` is what LM's loop calls too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AND AGAIN WHEN THE HULL CHANGES. A spawn-time check alone is wrong for any mission that
# re-hulls: Gamma with a Q seats every crew in a story ship MINUTES after spawn, so a crew
# that ends up in a Defiant spawned as an Excelsior and would never have been given the
# quantum rounds - measured, not guessed, by printing the loadout and finding the hull was
# still the roster's.
#
# `ship_hull_changed` is the library's own notification, emitted from `set_ship_data_key`,
# which is the single funnel every hull change passes through.
//shared/signal/ship_hull_changed
    tng_torp_grant(SHIP_ID)
    ->END


//spawn if has_role(SPAWNED_ID, "__player__")
    tng_torp_grant(SPAWNED_ID)
    ->END

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A TNG YARD MAKES TNG ROUNDS, and makes them fast enough to matter.
#
# LegendaryMissions' own station route sets every registered type on every station and
# does it after `await delay_sim(1)`, so this waits LONGER on purpose - landing after it
# rather than racing it. Two `//spawn` routes have no ordering between them; a delay is
# the only thing that makes 'after' mean after.
#
# Gated twice: `station`, and the mod's own sides (inside tng_station_setup_torpedoes).
# A TSN starbase in a stock mission is untouched however many TNG addons are loaded -
# which is the playtest's own condition, 'do not break the base game doing this'.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
//spawn if has_role(SPAWNED_ID, "station")
    await delay_sim(2)
    tng_station_status = tng_station_setup_torpedoes(SPAWNED_ID)
    # print, NOT log: log() is Python logging with no handler attached and is invisible
    # in the engine, and this line is how an operator sees a yard was reshaped at all.
    if tng_station_status:
        print(tng_station_status)
    ->END
